    "body": "Welcome to Neginato Mezora Neginato Mezora shows the weather for the places you save, with an emphasis on accuracy and on when it will rain . Every forecast is a blend of up to 13 forecast models from five free services (Open-Meteo, the US National Weather Service, MET Norway, the German weather service DWD via Bright Sky, and Environment Canada). The current conditions are grounded in live readings of nearby weather stations, and the forecast learns each place's local quirks from those stations. Start here Add a place: press \u2318N (or the + button) and type a city, street address, ZIP or postal code, landmark, or coordinates. See Adding & Managing Places . Read the forecast: select the place in the sidebar. The detail pane shows now, rain, air quality, clouds, the next 48 hours and the next days. See Reading the Forecast . Get more stations (optional): in the UK, the Netherlands, Norway, France and Spain, a free key from the national weather service adds its stations. See Free Keys for More Stations . What the app does for accuracy Layer What it does Learn more Model blend Up to 13 forecast models are combined hour by hour with a weighted median, with weights that depend on the region and on how far ahead the hour is (high-resolution national models lead the first hours; the best global models lead later). Data Sources & Weights , Algorithms 15-minute rain Where a 15-minute model is available (US, Canada, UK, Netherlands, Germany and much of Europe), the next 2 hours of rain are shown in 15-minute steps. Rain Graph & Bars Live stations Every station network that covers the place is read at each refresh (airports worldwide plus national, road-weather and research networks), the stations are tested against each other, and the trusted ones are blended into the \"now\" values. Live Station Observations Learned local corrections For each place and hour of the day, the app learns how far the models run from what close stations measure, and corrects the forecast temperatures, feels-like, highs and lows by up to \u00b14 \u00b0C (\u00b17 \u00b0F). Learned Local Corrections Air quality The nearest air-quality monitor's reading as reported (US and Canada), otherwise the CAMS air-quality forecast. Never estimated from the weather. Reading the Forecast Weather alerts The official warnings in force for the place, as its issuer published them: the national weather service in the US, Canada, Germany and Norway, MeteoAlarm in 35 more European countries and Israel. Shown on the forecast page and as a warning sign in the sidebar; never made up or estimated by the app. Weather Alerts Where things are Sidebar: your saved places (up to 50), each with its temperature in that place's own units, a rain hint and, when an official alert is in force, a warning sign. Drag to reorder; the \u2026 button names, moves or removes a place. Toolbar: + (add a place), refresh, the unit button ( \u00b0F / \u00b0C , the selected place's units), and the gear (Settings). Settings ( \u2318, ): four tabs: Sources , Weights , Stations and General . The app menu also has Data Sources & Weights\u2026 and Stations & Keys\u2026 , which open those tabs directly. Help ( \u2318? ): this book. The search field at the top left searches every page, and the Help menu opens the main pages directly. All help pages Adding & Managing Places Reading the Forecast Rain Graph & Bars Guide Weather Alerts Units, Refreshing & Offline Keyboard Shortcuts & Menus Settings: Data Sources & Weights Settings: Stations Free Keys for More Stations Learned Local Corrections Live Station Observations Ensemble Blending & Citations Privacy, Data & Storage Troubleshooting & FAQ"
