    "section": "Getting Started",
    "href": "shortcuts.html",
    "body": "Keyboard Shortcuts & Menus Shortcuts Shortcut Command \u2318N File \u203a Add a City\u2026 (opens the Add a city window) \u2318R View \u203a Refresh (the selected place) \u2318U View \u203a Switch Selected Place to Celsius / Fahrenheit: switches the selected place between \u00b0F and \u00b0C (with no place selected, Set Default Units to Celsius / Fahrenheit switches the default units for new places) \u2303\u2318S View \u203a Show/Hide Sidebar \u2318, Neginato Mezora \u203a Settings\u2026 (opens on the Sources tab) \u2318? ( \u21e7\u2318/ ) Help \u203a Neginato Mezora Help \u2318Q Quit (pending changes are saved first) \u2191 \u2193 Select the previous or next place in the sidebar Esc Close the Add a city window Return / Space In the Add a city window: add the highlighted result Menus Neginato Mezora: About Neginato Mezora; Settings\u2026 ( \u2318, , Sources tab); Data Sources & Weights\u2026 (the Weights tab); Stations & Keys\u2026 (the Stations tab); Quit. File: Add a City\u2026 ( \u2318N ). View: Refresh ( \u2318R ); Switch Selected Place to Celsius or Fahrenheit ( \u2318U ; with no place selected, Set Default Units to Celsius or Fahrenheit); Show/Hide Sidebar. Help: Neginato Mezora Help ( \u2318? ), then direct links to Reading the Forecast, the Rain Graph & Bars Guide, Data Sources & Blend Weights, Station Settings, Free Keys for More Stations, Live Station Observations, Learned Local Corrections, Forecast Algorithms & Citations, and Troubleshooting & FAQ. Toolbar Button What it does + Add a city ( \u2318N ). Refresh Refresh this place ( \u2318R ); dimmed while it loads or when offline. \u00b0F / \u00b0C Shows the selected place's unit; click to switch that place (with no place selected, the default units for new places). Its tooltip is the \u2318U title: Switch Selected Place to Celsius (or to Fahrenheit ), or with no place selected Set Default Units to Celsius (or to Fahrenheit ). Gear Settings ( \u2318, ). Each sidebar row's \u2026 button holds Name / Edit Location\u2026, Set Location Name, Move up, Move down and Remove (also available to VoiceOver as row actions). Rows have no right-click menu."
